========================================================================================
(1) EXHAUSTIVENESS: all integer classes with minD <= 8, over |x|,|y| <= 40
========================================================================================
  m004: 51 classes with minD<=8; farthest is at |.|=16 (box 40) -> the set is bounded and fully inside the box
      minD=0: 1 classes, max |.| = 0
      minD=2: 8 classes, max |.| = 4
      minD=4: 8 classes, max |.| = 8
      minD=6: 22 classes, max |.| = 12
      minD=8: 12 classes, max |.| = 16
  m003: 47 classes with minD<=8; farthest is at |.|=12 (box 40) -> the set is bounded and fully inside the box
      minD=0: 1 classes, max |.| = 0
      minD=2: 10 classes, max |.| = 3
      minD=4: 8 classes, max |.| = 6
      minD=6: 16 classes, max |.| = 9
      minD=8: 12 classes, max |.| = 12

========================================================================================
(2) BOTH DIRECTIONS: an integer class of one whose series occurs at NO integer class of the other
========================================================================================

  --- classes of m004 absent from m003 ---
    20 classes, 6 distinct series
      e.g. m004(-1, 0) (leading x^2; only 11 classes of m003 can compete, all checked):
           -2*q -2*q^2 +2*q^3 +8*q^4 +16*q^5 +16*q^6 +10*q^7 -14*q^8 -52*q^9 -102*q^10 -154*q^11 -192*q^12 -188*q^13 -116*q^14 +42*q^15
           attained on m004 at [(-1, 0), (1, 0)]
      e.g. m004(-3, -1) (leading x^4; only 19 classes of m003 can compete, all checked):
           +1*q^2 +1*q^3 +1*q^4 -1*q^5 -4*q^6 -10*q^7 -16*q^8 -22*q^9 -25*q^10 -19*q^11 +40*q^13 +100*q^14 +189*q^15
           attained on m004 at [(-3, -1), (-3, 1), (3, -1), (3, 1)]
      e.g. m004(-5, -1) (leading x^6; only 35 classes of m003 can compete, all checked):
           -1*q^3 -1*q^4 -2*q^5 -3*q^6 -3*q^7 -3*q^8 +6*q^10 +18*q^11 +33*q^12 +56*q^13 +80*q^14 +106*q^15
           attained on m004 at [(-5, -1), (-5, 1), (5, -1), (5, 1)]
      e.g. m004(-3, 0) (leading x^6; only 35 classes of m003 can compete, all checked):
           +2*q^3 +4*q^4 +6*q^5 +2*q^6 -4*q^7 -20*q^8 -42*q^9 -64*q^10 -82*q^11 -84*q^12 -52*q^13 +28*q^14 +158*q^15
           attained on m004 at [(-3, 0), (3, 0)]

  --- classes of m003 absent from m004 ---
    16 classes, 4 distinct series
      e.g. m003(-1, 1) (leading x^2; only 9 classes of m004 can compete, all checked):
           -1*q -1*q^2 +2*q^3 +7*q^4 +11*q^5 +11*q^6 +3*q^7 -17*q^8 -49*q^9 -88*q^10 -126*q^11 -148*q^12 -132*q^13 -57*q^14 +96*q^15
